![title-img](https://nsm09.casimages.com/img/2025/05/31//2505310207423242518595349.png)

The `ftxui::component` module defines the logic that produces interactive components that respond to user events (keyboard, mouse, etc.).

The [Example](module-component-examples.html) section provides a collection of examples.

A `ftxui::App` defines a main loop that renders a component.

A `[ftxui::Component](namespaceftxui.html#af1479ede01dbf087342534ab4ada11d3)` is a shared pointer to a `ftxui::ComponentBase`. The latter defines:

-   `ftxui::ComponentBase::Render()`: How to render the interface.
-   `ftxui::ComponentBase::OnEvent()`: How to react to events.
-   `ftxui::ComponentBase::Add()`: Construct a parent/child relationship between two components. The tree of components is used to define how to navigate using the keyboard.

`[ftxui::Element](namespaceftxui.html#a2bc31f2d685189e5c61d2293a1f51b4f)` are used to render a single frame.

`[ftxui::Component](namespaceftxui.html#af1479ede01dbf087342534ab4ada11d3)` are used to render dynamic user interface, producing multiple frame, and updating its state on events.

[Gallery](https://arthursonzogni.github.io/FTXUI/examples_2component_2gallery_8cpp-example.html) of multiple components. ([demo](https://arthursonzogni.github.io/FTXUI/examples/?file=component/gallery))

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4759106/147247330-b60beb9f-e665-48b4-81c0-4b01ee95bc66.png)

All predefined components are available in ["ftxui/dom/component.hpp"](./component_8hpp.html)

